    <meta name="description" content="About Dr. Lydia Moreno — associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at Riverbend University, with research in 
neural decoding, biomedical imaging, single-cell omics, and explainable AI.">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#102b3f">
    <title>About Me | Dr. Lydia Moreno</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/styles.css">
    <script src="assets/js/main.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="container header-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="index.html" aria-label="Dr. Lydia Moreno — home">
          <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">LM</span>
          <span class="brand-copy">
            <strong>Lydia Moreno</strong>
            <span>Computational Neuroscience</span>
          </span>
        </a>
        <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-nav">
          <span class="nav-toggle-lines" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="sr-only">Toggle navigation</span>
        </button>
        <nav class="site-nav" id="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
          <ul>
            <li><a href="about.html" aria-current="page">About Me</a></li>
            <li><a href="blog.html">Blog</a></li>
            <li><a href="publications.html">Publications</a></li>
            <li><a class="nav-contact" href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">Profile · Curriculum Vitae</p>
          <h1 id="page-title">About Me</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Computational neuroscientist, educator, and tool builder working to make complex
            neural and biomedical data explainable, useful, and reproducible.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="info.md" download>Download CV (Markdown)</a>
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="publications.html">Selected publications</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="biography-title">
        <div class="container about-grid">
          <div class="reveal">
            <p class="eyebrow">Biography</p>
            <h2 id="biography-title">Understanding how neural circuits encode the world.</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>
                Dr. Lydia Moreno is an associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at
                Riverbend University's School of Biological Sciences. Her work sits at the
                intersection of machine learning, systems neuroscience, and bioinformatics,
                aiming to unravel how neural circuits encode and process complex sensory information.
              </p>
              <p>
                She received her Ph.D. in Computational Biology from Baywood Institute of
                Technology and completed postdoctoral training in high-throughput imaging
                analysis at Northborough Research Center. Her research combines interpretable
                machine learning, graph-based representations, and scalable data pipelines to
                move from raw measurements toward mechanistic insight.
              </p>
              <p>
                Alongside her research program, Dr. Moreno teaches computational neuroscience
                and advanced machine-learning methods for biology, and mentors students working
                across neural data analysis, bioinformatics, and biomedical imaging.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <aside class="fact-card reveal" aria-label="Contact and academic details">
            <h3>Profile details</h3>
            <ul class="fact-list">
              <li><strong>Role</strong><span>Associate Professor of Computational Neuroscience</span></li>
              <li><strong>School</strong><span>School of Biological Sciences, Riverbend University</span></li>
              <li><strong>Office</strong><span>Blakely Hall, Room 312</span></li>
              <li><strong>Email</strong><span><a href="mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu">lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu</a></span></li>
              <li><strong>Profiles</strong><span><a href="https://twitter.com/LydiaNeuroLab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Twitter</a> · <a 
href="https://github.com/lydia-moreno" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a></span></li>
            </ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section--tinted" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Research Interests</p>
              <h2 id="research-title">Four connected research directions.</h2>
              <p>Each direction pairs a scientific question with a computational method.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card-grid">
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <h3>Neural Encoding &amp; Decoding</h3>
              <p>Developing interpretable models that translate spike-train data into behavioral predictions.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <h3>Machine Learning for Biomedical Imaging</h3>
              <p>Applying convolutional and graph neural networks to magnetic resonance and two-photon microscopy data.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
              <h3>Single-Cell Omics</h3>
              <p>Designing scalable pipelines for integrating multimodal single-cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
              <h3>Explainable AI in Neuroscience</h3>
              <p>Building frameworks to probe decision boundaries and feature attributions in black-box models.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Selected Projects</p>
              <h2 id="projects-title">Tools that turn data into scientific insight.</h2>
              <p>Collaborative work spanning imaging, connectomics, and single-cell biology.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="project-grid">
            <article class="project-card reveal">
              <p class="project-role">Lead Developer &amp; Project Coordinator</p>
              <h3>DeepVision: High-Resolution Neural Activity Mapping</h3>
              <ul class="clean-list">
                <li>Designed a PyTorch-based pipeline to segment two-photon images of mouse visual cortex.</li>
                <li>Integrated temporal convolutional networks to predict stimulus orientation from calcium-imaging traces.</li>
                <li>Deployed a Dockerized microservice for real-time data processing with Cascade Imaging Lab.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
            <article class="project-card reveal">
              <p class="project-role">Principal Investigator</p>
              <h3>NeuroGraph: Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis</h3>
              <ul class="clean-list">
                <li>Constructed graph representations of reconstructed neuron meshes from electron microscopy.</li>
                <li>Trained GNNs to classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs.</li>
                <li>Published an open-source toolkit in the NeuroTools suite, adopted by 12 labs worldwide.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
            <article class="project-card reveal">
              <p class="project-role">Co-Principal Investigator</p>
              <h3>CellMap: Multimodal Single-Cell Atlas</h3>
              <ul class="clean-list">
                <li>Developed a Nextflow workflow combining scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial FISH data.</li>
                <li>Implemented Bayesian clustering to resolve cell-type hierarchies in human cortical organoids.</li>
                <li>Presented at the International Conference on Single-Cell Genomics (ICSCG) 2023.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section--tinted" aria-labelledby="education-title">
        <div class="container about-grid">
          <div class="reveal">
            <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
            <h2 id="education-title">Training across computation and biology.</h2>
            <ol class="timeline">
              <li class="timeline-item">
                <p class="timeline-meta">2014–2019</p>
                <h3>Ph.D., Computational Biology</h3>
                <p>Baywood Institute of Technology</p>
                <p>Dissertation: “Deep Learning Models for Decoding Neural Population Activity”</p>
              </li>
              <li class="timeline-item">
                <p class="timeline-meta">2012–2014</p>
                <h3>M.Sc., Bioinformatics</h3>
                <p>Riverbend University</p>
                <p>Thesis: “Statistical Methods for Single-Cell RNA-Seq Analysis”</p>
              </li>
              <li class="timeline-item">
                <p class="timeline-meta">2008–2012</p>
                <h3>B.Sc., Computer Science</h3>
                <p>Crestfield College of Engineering</p>
                <p>Graduated magna cum laude; President, Data Science Club</p>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal">
            <p class="eyebrow">Teaching &amp; Mentorship</p>
            <h2>Building the next generation of computational scientists.</h2>
            <ul class="clean-list">
              <li><strong>Undergraduate Course:</strong> “Introduction to Computational Neuroscience” (Spring 2025)</li>
              <li><strong>Graduate Seminar:</strong> “Advanced Machine Learning Methods in Biology” (Fall 2024)</li>
              <li><strong>Mentorship:</strong> Supervised 8 Ph.D. students and 12 Master's theses on topics ranging from neural data analysis to bioinformatics 
pipelines.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="skills-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Skills &amp; Tools</p>
              <h2 id="skills-title">A practical computational toolkit.</h2>
              <p>Languages, frameworks, data systems, and visualization tools used across the lab.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card-grid">
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <h3>Languages</h3>
              <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Programming languages">
                <li>Python</li><li>R</li><li>C++</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <h3>Frameworks</h3>
              <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Machine learning frameworks">
                <li>PyTorch</li><li>TensorFlow</li><li>scikit-learn</li><li>NetworkX</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <h3>Data Tools</h3>
              <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Data and infrastructure tools">
                <li>Nextflow</li><li>Snakemake</li><li>Docker</li><li>Kubernetes</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
            <article class="info-card reveal">
              <h3>Analysis &amp; Visualization</h3>
              <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Analysis and visualization tools">
                <li>MATLAB</li><li>Jupyter</li><li>Seurat</li><li>Scanpy</li><li>D3.js</li><li>Plotly</li><li>Matplotlib</li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section--tinted" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="contact-panel reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
              <h2 id="contact-title">Start a conversation.</h2>
              <p>
                For research collaborations, talks, student supervision, or questions about
                the lab's software, please get in touch by email.
              </p>
              <p>Blakely Hall, Room 312<br>Riverbend University</p>
            </div>
            <div class="contact-links">
              <a class="contact-link" href="mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu">
                <span>Email</span><strong>lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu</strong>
              </a>
              <a class="contact-link" href="https://twitter.com/LydiaNeuroLab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <span>Twitter</span><strong>@LydiaNeuroLab</strong>
